/**
 * @mainpage MIDILAR
 *
 * MIDILAR is the MIDI layer of the RoModular ecosystem: MIDI 1.0 and MIDI 2.0
 * protocol, messages, parsing, routing and real-time devices for desktop and
 * embedded targets, built on Foundation (general utilities) and MCC (music
 * theory). MIDI 2.0 Universal MIDI Packets are the internal model; MIDI 1.0
 * byte streams are translated at the edges.
 *
 * @note Version 0.2.0 is the first release of the rebuilt library, prepared
 * on the `rebuild` branch; it merges into `main` after hardware validation.
 *
 * @section MIDILARMainModules Modules
 *
 * - @ref MIDILAR_Core "Core": MIDILAR, MCC and Foundation version information.
 * - @ref MIDILAR_Protocol "Protocol": channels, groups, values, UMP packets,
 *   MIDI 1.0 and USB MIDI 1.0 translation, MIDI Time Code and MCC pitch
 *   conversions.
 * - @ref MIDILAR_Devices "Devices": filters, transforms, scale filter and
 *   chord generation, router, MIDI clock, step sequencer and MTC.
 *
 * Hardware transports are separate libraries built on the Protocol
 * conversions. The rules MIDILAR types follow are collected in the
 * @ref MIDILAR_Specification "MIDI-Domain Specification".
 *
 * @section MIDILARMainDependency Dependencies
 *
 * MIDILAR links `Foundation::Foundation` (Foundation 1.4 or a newer 1.x
 * release) and `MCC::MCC` (MCC 0.5.2 or a newer 0.x release). It uses local
 * packages when available and otherwise fetches the pinned releases from
 * GitHub; see @ref MIDILAR_BuildGuide_Dependency.
 */
